ansi-font-family:Calibri;\r\n	mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;\r\n	mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";\r\n	mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\n	mso-fareast-language:EN-US;}\r\n</style>\r\n<![endif]-->\r\n\r\n</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">In two of the biggest economies, namely UK and US, the\r\ndeath rate is still rising, although the rate of increase is going down. The\r\nCentre of Disease Control for US and the Chief Medical Attorney have all\r\nindicated that the peak in the US could be between 16<sup>th</sup> to the 19<sup>th</sup>\r\nApril 2020. These dates could see incredible RALLIES, however, bear in mind\r\nthat this is a bear market rally in phase 2 which I will talk about later.\r\nThese projections are based on calculations from the boffins at MIT and other\r\nprediction agencies so there is a lot of analysis behind it. A simpler way to\r\nfollow this is to see what’s happening in China. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-no-proof:yes"><img src="file:///C:\\Users\\robst\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\msohtmlclip1\\01\\clip_image002.png" width="602" height="276"></span><br>\r\n</p><p class="MsoNormal"><img style="width: 100%;" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," data-filename="3D_medical_animation_coronavirus_structure.jpg"><br></p><p class="MsoNormal"><br>\r\n<span style="font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">Now\r\nthe Province of Wuhan is relaxing its lockdown of 72 days, which has seen\r\ninfection rates and deaths near zero. The relaxed measures will allow the\r\npeople of the province to travel around China. All eyes should be on China as\r\nthis is a leading indicator of what will happen in the rest of the world. All\r\nyou must do is look at China and imagine that you will enter this scenario in\r\napproximately 4 to 5 weeks. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;mso-no-proof:yes"><img src="file:///C:\\Users\\robst\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\msohtmlclip1\\01\\clip_image004.png" width="335" height="295"></span><span style="font-size:12.0pt;\r\nline-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:\r\n&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;">Reinfections are key, as I said this is not a linear\r\ndisease, it is like a diminishing sign wave (SEE ABOVE) which will rise and\r\nfall in lower magnitudes until Social Distancing or a vaccine is produced. In\r\nterms of market talk, in the short term we should see a rally (The Suckers\r\nbeing pulled in), in the longer term the trend is down when the bear market\r\nreally takes its shape, expect money to be printed left right and centre as\r\ncentral banks hope to revive the economies and pray that hyperinflation does\r\nnot raise its ugly head like it Did in West Germany during WW2.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><br></p>', 'test-its-still-about-covid-19-dont-get-sick-of-this-virus-2020-04-08-5e8dd3d4cfd5a.png', '2020-04-08 13:38:28', '2020-04-08 13:38:28');
