ont-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">price </span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">crept </span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">back up on early UK market open. But\r\nexpecting it to fall back</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">… to\r\naround $24 at most. </span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-US;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">I\'ve put some Trades on Virtual Portfolio to monitor, as I am not going to short Oil as it is too strong a commodity. The Virtual Trade is for learning, I want to see how the option prices behave as Oil price recedes.<br></span></p>', 'oil-price-recedes-as-expected-target-24-2020-04-14-5e956e05c4a0b.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-14 08:02:13', '2020-04-14 08:02:13'),
	(66, 17, 4, 'Will Oil Fall Further to $20 again?', NULL, 'will-oil-fall-further-to-20-again-', '<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">I\'ve had a lot of beginners luck coming back into trading after 10 years of absence.</span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">I can see an Inverted </span><span style="font-size:\r\n18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">penant</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"> Chart pattern. Although it’s hard to tell which way</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"> the price will break out of this </span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">penant</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">,\r\ngiven the fundamentals and lacklustre results from the oil cuts, I would expect oil to\r\nfall to around $18-$20 range.</span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">I will be looking to open a position at $20 again. <br></span>\r\n\r\n</p>', 'will-oil-fall-further-to-20-again-2020-04-14-5e956e8988b4a.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-14 08:04:25', '2020-04-14 08:04:25'),
	(67, 17, 5, 'Gold Breaking Resistance As I Write This', NULL, 'gold-breaking-resistance-as-i-write-this', '<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:16.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">Gold is about to head into new territory,\r\nand most likely exceed the highs of 2011.</span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:16.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:16.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">Given the market has more to fall yet as\r\nthe ripple effects are realised, gold should easily reach levels around $2000\r\nif not more. </span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:16.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:16.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">In 2008-2011 we saw gold double.<span style="mso-spacerun:yes">&nbsp; </span>That would be the equivalent of seeing gold\r\ngo from around $1400 to $2800!</span></p>', 'gold-breaking-resistance-as-i-write-this-2020-04-14-5e956ed4ba38c.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-14 08:05:40', '2020-04-14 08:05:40'),
	(71, 17, 4, 'Oil Technical Divergence - Watch Out For This', NULL, 'oil-technical-divergence-watch-out-for-this', '<p>I wanted to point something out to help you prepare for a trade. This might happen or might not... but more often than not, it does happen. </p><p><br></p><p>See the chart above.... observer the MACD and RSI. </p><p>As Oil heads lower below $20, notice if the MACD histogram, and RSI levels remain at level higher than the previous bottom at $20. </p><p><br></p><p>What this essentially means is that at the lower price, there is more strenght in the market so to speak, and we call this a technical divergence which signals "weaker bears" and usually, the "bulls take over" and the price starts rising. </p><p><br></p><p>Here\'s an old example of divergence and you can see the price start moving up once the divergence is achieved. Check out the Learning Center for lessons on Divergence patterns.</p><p><br></p><p><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""><img style="width: 1006px;" src="data:image/png;base64," data-filename="image.png"></p>', 'oil-technical-divergence-watch-out-for-this-2020-04-15-5e96e9efccbd2.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-15 11:03:11', '2020-04-15 11:03:11'),
	(72, 17, 4, 'Inverted Penant Chart Pattern on Oil Again - Very Short Term', NULL, 'inverted-penant-chart-pattern-on-oil-again-very-short-term', '<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">Another few days of uncertainty and oil\r\nswinging sideways in a narrow range. Creating another inverted </span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">penant</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">\r\nchart pattern… expect a breakout shortly….</span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">Based on previous </span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">analysis</span><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">,\r\nthis should be a downward breakout heading towards $17-$18. </span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;mso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\ncolor:black;mso-color-index:1;mso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;\r\nmso-style-textfill-type:solid;mso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;mso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">But I would take caution at those price\r\nlevels, oil could bounce back almost immediately. </span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size:18.0pt;\r\nfont-family:Calibri;mso-ascii-font-family:Calibri;mso-fareast-font-family:+mn-ea;\r\nmso-bidi-font-family:+mn-cs;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-fareast;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;color:black;mso-color-index:1;\r\nmso-font-kerning:12.0pt;language:en-GB;mso-style-textfill-type:solid;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-themecolor:text1;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:black;\r\nmso-style-textfill-fill-alpha:100.0%">**NOTE: this could easily be an upward breakout if there is any strong fundamental news coming out. For instance Mr Trump sending another tweet to influence oil price, who knows maybe this time he could say "we\'re cutting down on our production"!<br></span></p>', 'inverted-penant-chart-pattern-on-oil-again-very-short-term-2020-04-16-5e9837989ace2.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-16 10:46:48', '2020-04-16 10:46:48'),
	(73, 17, 4, 'Oil Falls Beyond Expectation - now at $12.40! (WTI Spot price)', NULL, 'oil-falls-beyond-expectation-now-at-12-40-wti-spot-price-', '<p>Hi All, </p><p><br></p><p>I wanted to quickly give you an update on what happened to the chart pattern I showed on the previous post. </p><p>As you can see Oil did head down comfortably, and there was some turbulence around $18 before continuing. </p><p><br></p><p>However, it has fallen beyond my expectation, I am shocked that WTI spot price could fall as low as $12.40 (as at the time of taking the chart today). My expectation as $15 at worst. </p><p><br></p><p>So why is this happening? To be honest, I can\'t understand for sure, but the May Oil contracts are due to expire tomorrow (as I learn today), and with an oversupply in the market, there is a storage problem. Thus traders are essentially offloading at whatever price they can so they don\'t have to take delivery and store the oil. </p><p><br></p><p>It all sounds confusing I know, and the purpose of this post is not to go into the logistical ins and outs of physical oil trading. But the key thing to watch out for next is the June future prices, which are around $10 more! Normally the prices would have converged by now, but now we have a situation known as Contango, where the future price is far higher than the current spot price, thus giving this huge gap in the oil price.<b> I am really keen to see what happens over the next 2 days as the May contracts expire and the June contracts kick in. </b></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 'oil-falls-beyond-expectation-now-at-1240-wti-spot-price-2020-04-20-5e9d9f75ca6a2.jpg', NULL, '2020-04-20 13:11:17', '2020-04-20 13:11:17'),
	(78, 17, 4, 'Possible Head & Shoulders Chart Pattern on Crude Oil', NULL, 'possible-head-shoulders-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil', '<p>Crude oils recent rally is peaking as the June contract expiry nears. A \r\npossible head and shoulders or triangular chart pattern is forming. Lets\r\n monitor this for our next big trade.</p>', 'possible-head-shoulders-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil-2020-05-07-5eb40ad51a746.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hJQ_Zbux2k', '2020-05-07 13:19:17', '2020-05-07 13:19:17'),
	(81, 17, 4, 'Crude Oil Slumps to ZERO!', NULL, 'crude-oil-slumps-to-zero-', '<p>A shocking moment for the world. No investor or trader has ever seen this in his lifetime, WTI Oil for May 2020 Delivery slumped to zero and below as everyone started dumping their trades on fear that they would not find storage due to the oversupply. Watch the video to see how it panned out as I sat there all day watching oil fall. <br></p>', 'crude-oil-slumps-to-zero-2020-05-08-5eb5066430810.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jWJbRBsexRk', '2020-05-08 07:12:36', '2020-05-08 07:12:36'),
	(82, 17, 4, 'I Lost 53% of my Portfolio Today due to ONE MISTAKE', NULL, 'i-lost-53-of-my-portfolio-today-due-to-one-mistake', '<p>It was all going well, my portfolio was up 33% since starting with £5000 only. But today I made one trade that was executed wrongly for a Crude Oil position, which put my \r\naccount into a margin call, and all my great trades were closed out.</p><p><br></p><p>Click the video above to see a demo of what happened as I recorded everything so that we can all learn from this mistake. <br></p>', 'i-lost-53-of-my-portfolio-today-due-to-one-mistake-2020-05-08-5eb5077795a89.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sBXKMBBfch4', '2020-05-08 07:17:11', '2020-05-08 07:17:11'),
	(83, 17, 4, 'Crude Oil Slides 30% on USO Fund Sale', NULL, 'crude-oil-slides-30-on-uso-fund-sale', '<p>We thought Crude Oil was going to rally, we had very strong technical divergences, BUT... suddenly crude oil reversed from around $17 and headed back towards $10 a barrell. Took us by surprise causing us to make rash decisions and losing out on some great Long trades! Click the video above for a full explanation and my next steps. <br></p>', 'crude-oil-slides-30-on-uso-fund-sale-2020-05-08-5eb509797cf11.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ppvtgyNGq0U', '2020-05-08 07:25:45', '2020-05-08 07:25:45'),
	(84, 17, 4, 'I failed to Profit from the Big Rally in Crude Oil - Here\'s Why', NULL, 'i-failed-to-profit-from-the-big-rally-in-crude-oil-here-s-why', '<p>I calculated this rally correctly. But i mismanaged the situation and \r\nended up making Nothing on this Crude Oil rally from $10 to $25. Find \r\nout why i failed and learn from this mistake, click the video above to learn more. <br></p>', 'i-failed-to-profit-from-the-big-rally-in-crude-oil-heres-why-2020-05-08-5eb509f3b0c3e.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q-_scVCMLtE', '2020-05-08 07:27:47', '2020-05-08 07:27:47'),
	(85, 17, 4, 'Possible Head & Shoulders Chart Pattern on Crude Oil', NULL, 'possible-head-shoulders-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil', '<p>Crude oils recent rally is peaking as the June contract expiry nears. A \r\npossible head and shoulders or triangular chart pattern is forming. Or it could be a triangular pattern if the Oil price is dragged down to around $6 on 20th June and we see a repeat of the oil price crash. Check the video above to learn more about my speculation on this. <br></p>', 'possible-head-shoulders-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil-2020-05-08-5eb50a9f749c0.JPG', 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_hJQ_Zbux2k', '2020-05-08 07:30:39', '2020-05-08 07:30:39'),
	(86, 17, 4, 'Prepare to Trade Crude Oil now. Crude Oil is Moving Sideways', NULL, 'prepare-to-trade-crude-oil-now-crude-oil-is-moving-sideways', '<p>Crude oil rallied from $10 to $25 - for no apparent reason. Now its been\r\n consolidating around $25 for almost 7 days, a break out is around the \r\ncorner, which way will it move?</p><p><br></p><p>Click the video above to see my take on this. <br></p>', 'prepare-to-trade-crude-oil-now-crude-oil-is-moving-sideways-2020-05-13-5ebbf304cb9f0.JPG', 'https://youtu.be/yXEQzvxfUVU', '2020-05-13 13:15:48', '2020-05-13 13:15:48'),
	(87, 17, 4, 'Triangular Chart Pattern on Crude Oil as Price Consolidates', NULL, 'triangular-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil-as-price-consolidates', '<p>WTI and Brent Crude have been moving sideways for almost 7 days now. Literally no action in the oil market. The trading range has become incredibly narrow now, and my judgement tells me we are about to have a break-out, within this week before Friday 15th May!</p><p><br></p><p>But.. I am quite perplexed as to which way the breakout will be. Both the WTI and Brent Oil charts are forming 2 different triangular chart patterns. What could this mean? Does this mean the price of WTI crude oil and brent will diverge again like 20th May 2020?</p><p><br></p><p>I\'m struggling to judge this one, so the best thing for me to do is trade an Options Straddle position with a Call and a Put. Whichever way the breakout happens, I should end up with a profit. I will heavy on the down-side as I am more inclined that Oil should fall running up to the June contract expiry. </p><p><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""></p>', 'triangular-chart-pattern-on-crude-oil-as-price-consolidates-2020-05-13-5ebbf45422925.jpg', NULL, '2020-05-13 13:21:24', '2020-05-13 13:21:24'),
	(88, 17, 5, 'Time to Buy LONG on Gold at $1700', NULL, 'time-to-buy-long-on-gold-at-1700', '<p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="background-color: inherit;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">The time has come to go LONG on\r\nGold. </span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="background-color: inherit;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">It’s been moving sideways similar\r\nto oil for some time now, forming a </span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">penant</span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">\r\nchart pattern – ready to break upwards now. </span></span></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="background-color: inherit;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">Expect gold to rally to around\r\n$1850 initially. </span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="background-color: inherit;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">This should coincide with market\r\nturmoil as investors shift out of other assets and move into gold AGAIN.</span></span></p>', 'time-to-buy-long-on-gold-at-1700-2020-05-14-5ebce621d551e.jpg', NULL, '2020-05-14 06:33:05', '2020-05-14 06:33:05'),
	(89, 17, 6, 'Stock Markets at Resistance - Time to Fall again', NULL, 'stock-markets-at-resistance-time-to-fall-again', '<blockquote class="blockquote"><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">Markets rally has been slowing down. </span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">Last night the FED gave a speech which signalled more turbulence to come, which of course is naturally expected, as the effects of COVID-19 lockdowns have not materialised yet. </span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;"><br></span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">SPX starts it reversal AT the </span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">ema</span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">(200)\r\nwhich also coincides with a Resistance Line we have. </span></p><p style="language:en-GB;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-left:0in;\r\ntext-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed;mso-line-break-override:none;\r\nword-break:normal;punctuation-wrap:hanging"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">Expect SPX to continue falling to\r\nthe next support level of 2600, </span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">albiet</span><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Calibri;">\r\nrather slowly. </span></p></blockquote>', 'stock-markets-at-resistance-time-to-fall-again-2020-05-14-5ebce71f6f6d7.jpg', NULL, '2020-05-14 06:37:19', '2020-05-14 06:37:19'),
	(90, 17, 4, 'Crude Oil Ready to Slump again for June Contracts', NULL, 'crude-oil-ready-to-slump-again-for-june-contracts', '<p>I woke up this morning to an announcement from CTFC (Commodity Futures Trading Commission) which is the regulator for commidities trading, in which they issues a WARNING to brokers, trading houses et al that Oil prices may go negative again running up to the June Contract expiry on 19th June 2020, which is next Tuesday (today is Thursday 14th May).</p><p><br></p><p>They also mention this is not investment advice, this is merely warning so that trading houses can take precautions, to&nbsp; prevent huge losses for investors etc. But lets face it, this is just admitting that there is a very high probability that oil prices&nbsp; - that is the spot cash price for WTI crude, will go negative again. </p><p><br></p><p>So this was reassuring given that i been waiting almost a month for this to materialise, and recently oil\'s been moving sideways fro the last 9 days which has been perplexing me. </p><p>I\'ve been following the oil chart like a hawk, but nothing seems to be happening. But today it got me thinking...all this while i was looking at the hourly chart to find the finer detail cos i usually use hourly chart after seeing the broader daily chart. But there is too much noise on the hourly chart, and it\'s not obvious what is happening. </p><p><br></p><p>So today I decided to zoom out into 4 hourly chart to eliminate most of the noise shown on hourly, and bingo! It became very obvious that "it is happening again".</p><p><br></p><p>Check out the chart above, you will see we have the same chart pattern formation, same technical indicator formation as the run up to 20th May 2020 when crude oil plummeted. </p><p><br></p><p>It is time to go in SHORT now. HOWEVER... keep in mind there will be systems in place to try and support the price of oil this time. They may have circuit breakers to suspend trading. Brokers and Trading Houses may set limits on how much shorting can be done, and may not even let you. My CMC Markets trading platform doesnt even let me short WTI cash anymore. </p><p><br></p><p>Good luck and invest Safely.</p><p><br></p><p>The black chart above is for BRENT Crude Oil, and the one below is for WTI crude oil</p><p><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt=""></p>', 'crude-oil-ready-to-slump-again-for-june-contracts-2020-05-14-5ebcebeeaaa1a.jpg', NULL, '2020-05-14 06:54:00', '2020-05-14 06:54:00'),
	(94, 17, 6, 'S&P500 Put Options show Abnormally High Volume', NULL, 's-p500-put-options-show-abnormally-high-volume', '<p>Here is something interesting I noticed last night. </p><p><br></p><p>The May Put with Strike 2800 showed extremely high trading volume. It looks like some institution is buying a lot of Puts? or selling a lot of puts? I don\'t have the detailed data at hand so I can only speculate what it is.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>What do you guys think is happening here? Is there a signal here that there might be a dramatic increase in S&amp;P500 Puts - thus markets are expected to fall anytime now?</p><p><br></p><p>Share your thoughts, and let see how this unravels.<br></p>', 'sp500-put-options-show-abnormally-high-volume-2020-05-22-5ec791b2e0334.jpg', NULL, '2020-05-22 08:47:46', '2020-05-22 08:47:46');
